***************************************************************** 2434 1451
    Covariances for Cr-53, S. Hoblit, BNL, Aug. 2011              2434 1451
                                                                  2434 1451
The COMMARA-2.0 covariances in the fast neutron region were       2434 1451
adopted for ENDF/B-VII.1. These covariances used the ENDF/B-VI.8  2434 1451
evaluation as the starting point. The reason was that both the    2434 1451
basic files (adopted by ENDF/B-VII.0) and covariances were        2434 1451
produced by the highly experience ORNL group, Hetrick etal (1991) 2434 1451
We restored these covariances although CSEWG decided to drop them 2434 1451
from ENDF/B-VII.0. In case of Cr the justification for dropping   2434 1451
was relatively weak and mostly concerned the resonance region.    2434 1451
At inelastic scattering threshold region, the original            2434 1451
ENDF/B-VI.8 uncertainties were increased based on the dispersion  2434 1451
analysis of existing evaluations. Similarly, capture cross        2434 1451
sections uncertainties at high energies were increased to values  2434 1451
that were deemed to be more realistic.                            2434 1451
                                                                  2434 1451
An MF33 LB=5 section was added to the covariances for elastic     2434 1451
scattering at the upper end of the resonance region (1 - 564 keV) 2434 1451
to account for the uncertainty in the scattering radius R'. The   2434 1451
uncertainty in R' was taken from the Atlas of Neutron Resonances  2434 1451
and propagated to the elastic cross sections, using the 33-group  2434 1451
energy bins of the AFCI COMMARA-2.0 processed files.              2434 1451
                                                                  2434 1451
***************************************************************** 2434 1451
 24-Cr- 53 ORNL Resonance Evaluation Including Covariance         2434 1451
                                                                  2434 1451
 L. C. Leal, H. Derrien, K. Guber, G. Arbanas and D. Wiarda       2434 1451
                                                                  2434 1451
 Resolved resonance parameter evaluation for Cr-53 was done with  2434 1451
the computer code SAMMY.[La03] Capture and transmission           2434 1451
measurements enriched Cr-53 and natural chromium were performed   2434 1451
at the Oak Ridge Electron Linear Accelerator (ORELA) of the Oak   2434 1451
Ridge National Laboratory. The neutron transmission and capture   2434 1451
data were measured in the energy range from 10 keV to 600 keV.    2434 1451
The transmission data were measured at the 80-meter flight-path,  2434 1451
whereas the 40-meter flight-path was used for the capture cross   2434 1451
section measurements. The determination of the resolved resonance 2434 1451
parameters for the chromium isotope below 100 keV relied mainly   2434 1451
on the recent ORELA measurements. The ORELA capture cross section 2434 1451
data were essential in the evaluation since there are no capture  2434 1451
cross section data available in the literature. In                2434 1451
addition to the new ORELA measurements, existing high-resolution  2434 1451
transmission data for enriched nuclides were also included in the 2434 1451
evaluation. Thermal cross section data available in the EXFOR data2434 1451
system were also included in the evaluation.                      2434 1451
                                                                  2434 1451
 Direct-semidirect (DSD) capture on Cr-53 was computed using the  2434 1451
computer code CUPIDO created by F.S. Dietrich (LLNL).[Pa95]  To   2434 1451
obtain the optical potential for this computation, the global     2434 1451
optical potential of Koning-Delaroche was manually adjusted to    2434 1451
reproduce the experimentally measured scattering radius R'.       2434 1451
This method was justified since low-energy phenomena are          2434 1451
determined by R'.  It was found that the low-energy capture is    2434 1451
dominated by electric-dipole (E1) capture of s-wave neutrons.  A  2434 1451
density form of the E1 operator was used.  The spectroscopic      2434 1451
factors for the capturing bound states in Cr-54 were taken from   2434 1451
W. Gongqing.[ND87] The computed thermal DSD capture is about 0.32 2434 1451
barns.  The uncertainty of DSD computation is inherently large,   2434 1451
usually about 20-30%.                                             2434 1451
                                                                  2434 1451
 A set of resonance parameter describing the experimental data    2434 1451
was obtained. Resonance parameter covariance matrices were also   2434 1451
obtained in the SAMMY evaluation process. The Cr-53 evaluation was2434 1451
done in the energy region 10-5 eV 564 keV.                        2434 1451
  Thermal cross section obtained in the present evaluation are    2434 1451
compared to the values listed in the Atlas of Neutron Resoances   2434 1451
in the following table:                                           2434 1451
                                                                  2434 1451
    Cross Section            ORNL                      Atlas      2434 1451
                   Resonance     Res+Direct                       2434 1451
       Capt       18.09+/-0.50     18.41            18.60+/-0.60  2434 1451
       Total      26.07+/-0.54     26.39            26.38+/-0.62  2434 1451
       Scat        7.98+/-0.36       -               7.78+/-0.20  2434 1451
                                                                  2434 1451
 Uncertainty in the group cross section around the thermal cross  2434 1451
section due the covariance data has been calculated for a energy  2434 1451
group between the energies 0.0253 eV and 0.3 eV. The average cross2434 1451
sections for this energy group are listed in the following tale:  2434 1451
                                                                  2434 1451
            Cross Section                Average Value            2434 1451
                                                                  2434 1451
                Capt                  17.32+/-0.48 (2.8%)         2434 1451
                Total                 26.07+/-0.51 (2.0%)         2434 1451
                Scat                   7.89+/-0.37 (4.7%)         2434 1451
                                                                  2434 1451
