        PRODUCT.  ISOTROPY IS ASSUMED.                            2434 1451
 12-51 THROUGH 12-63 BRANCHING RATIOS FOR THE LEVELS, COMPILED    2434 1451
        BY SHIBATA AND HETRICK [Sh87], ARE GIVEN.                 2434 1451
 12-102 (N,G) CAPTURE;  TNG CALCULATED.                           2434 1451
 14-51 THROUGH 14-58 AND 14-102 GAMMA RAY ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS   2434 1451
        ASSUMED TO BE ISOTROPIC.                                  2434 1451
 15-102 (N,G) CAPTURE;  TNG CALCULATED.                           2434 1451
                                                                  2434 1451
--------------------------------------------------------------    2434 1451
UNCERTAINTY FILES                                                 2434 1451
        AN LB=8 SECTION IS INCLUDED FOR ALL NON-DERIVED FILES AS  2434 1451
        REQUIRED BY ENDF/B-VI.                                    2434 1451
                                                                  2434 1451
 33-1   UNCERTAINTIES ARE DERIVED FROM 1.E-5 TO 10 EV.  FROM 10   2434 1451
        EV TO 20 MEV THEY ARE EXPLICIT, USING LB=0,1 AND 8.       2434 1451
 33-2   FROM 1.E-5 TO 10 EV, UNCERTAINTIES ARE EXPLICIT, BASED    2434 1451
        UPON THERMAL UNCERTAINTY AND OTHER DATA.  FROM 10 EV TO   2434 1451
        20 MEV THE FILES ARE DERIVED.                             2434 1451
 33-3   FROM 1.E-5 TO 200 KEV UNCERTAINTIES ARE DERIVED.  FROM 2002434 1451
        KEV TO 20 MEV UNCERTAINTIES ARE EXPLICIT, USING LB=1 AND 82434 1451
 33-4   UNCERTAINTIES ARE ALL DERIVED.                            2434 1451
 33-16  UNCERTAINTIES FOR (N,2N) ARE EXPLICIT, ESTIMATED FROM TNG 2434 1451
 33-22  UNCERTAINTIES FOR (N,NA) ARE EXPLICIT, ESTIMATED FROM TNG 2434 1451
 33-28  UNCERTAINTIES FOR (N,NP) ARE EXPLICIT, ESTIMATED FROM TNG 2434 1451
 33-51-91  UNCERTAINTIES FOR INELASTIC SCATTERING ARE EXPLICIT,   2434 1451
           BASED ON DATA AND CALCULATION UNCERTAINTIES.           2434 1451
 33-102 UNCERTAINTIES ARE EXPLICIT, BASED ON THERMAL DATA AT LOW  2434 1451
        ENERGIES, AND CALCULATED RESULTS ABOVE 200 KEV.           2434 1451
 33-103 UNCERTAINTIES ESTIMATED FROM TNG.                         2434 1451
 33-107 UNCERTAINTIES ESTIMATED FROM TNG.                         2434 1451
